WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.700
SpaceX lofted Turkey's first homegrown satellite while an xai data center lawsuit advanced in court. This is SpaceX Daily Episode 138. Starship's next flight window, a space force manifest scramble, and an engineering deep dive on falcon heavy side boosters are the run from here. Turkey's independent space program just logged an early on orbit milestone, according to defense here. The satellite's job is national communications and a technology demonstration.

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:34.573
SpaceX said a November window for Starship Flight 15, Tesla Roddy reports.

00:00:35.233 --> 00:00:40.713
The profile adds expanded test objectives for the Starship upper stage and the super heavy booster.

00:00:41.313 --> 00:00:45.013
Preparations continue at Starbase for the next integrated test campaign.

00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:52.599
The U.S. Space Force is adjusting mission planning after SpaceX retires a primary launch vehicle according to Politico.

00:00:53.159 --> 00:00:57.519
The retirement affects payload manifest scheduling and national security launch cadence.

00:00:57.519 --> 00:01:02.359
Officials are evaluating alternative vehicles and timelines for the missions that just

00:01:02.359 --> 00:01:03.379
lost that rocket.

00:01:04.304 --> 00:01:09.164
Litigation over the power plant feeding an XAI data center is moving ahead in federal

00:01:09.164 --> 00:01:10.964
court, DigWatch reports.

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:16.444
The case centers on environmental and permitting questions tied to the facility's energy supply.

00:01:17.084 --> 00:01:20.824
Proceedings will test whether existing approvals meet regulatory standards.

00:01:21.764 --> 00:01:27.464
Memphis and South Haven now carry a 20% salary increase for SpaceX staff willing to relocate.

00:01:27.464 --> 00:01:33.404
business today reports. The incentive supports expanded artificial intelligence work, or AI,

00:01:33.904 --> 00:01:40.004
at facilities linked to XAI infrastructure. Relocation targets roles tied to compute and satellite

00:01:40.004 --> 00:01:46.436
integration projects. Cursor and GitHub co-pilot are being scored against each other on code completion,

00:01:47.016 --> 00:01:53.296
agent workflows, and integration depth according to tech buzz. Cursor's shadow workspace, a hidden working

00:01:53.296 --> 00:01:56.916
copy of the project is getting attention from multi-file edits.

00:01:57.436 --> 00:02:01.276
The review weighs developer productivity gains against model rooting choices.

00:02:02.407 --> 00:02:07.867
Authentication, network controls, and workspace isolation are the focus of a new cursor dashboard

00:02:07.867 --> 00:02:10.047
hardening guide, according to Shattered.

00:02:10.687 --> 00:02:13.807
The sequence's 12 steps meant to be finished in 60 minutes.

00:02:14.447 --> 00:02:18.647
Implementation targets enterprise deployment practices for AI coding tools.

00:02:18.647 --> 00:02:23.630
Grand Vest Financial Group acquired SpaceX shares, market-beat reports.

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:28.930
The details appear in the latest 13F filing, the quarterly public report of holdings.

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:32.630
The purchase adds to institutional positions in the public company.

00:02:33.591 --> 00:02:40.511
In fresh filings, diversified advisory services reported a new position of 12,292 SpaceX shares.

00:02:41.231 --> 00:02:47.091
Sumitomo Mitsui DS asset management disclosed a purchase of 9,096 SpaceX shares.

00:02:47.091 --> 00:02:52.649
People on Reddit's SpaceX Lounge swapped notes on viewing spots and traffic for upcoming

00:02:52.649 --> 00:02:57.109
Boca Chica launches, and that is fan discussion rather than an official plan.

00:02:57.589 --> 00:03:01.469
The thread recommended Austin Departures and flagged local road closures.

00:03:02.049 --> 00:03:06.989
Contributors on Reddit examined zero-G refueling methods for Starship, including whether

00:03:06.989 --> 00:03:11.389
the vehicle would need to spin or use other propellant management techniques, and that

00:03:11.389 --> 00:03:12.929
remains enthusiast analysis.

00:03:12.929 --> 00:03:18.409
NASA's Space Flight reported that China has completed its first reflight of a flown booster.

00:03:18.929 --> 00:03:24.429
Progress is also underway toward recovering the Changjiang-Jing-12A first stage on a second attempt.

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:31.970
Worth keeping an eye on, plaintiffs argue that permitting for that XAI power plant did not fully address local impacts.

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:37.030
Resolution depends on forthcoming regulatory reviews and court findings on compliance.

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:41.730
The outcome could affect construction timelines for the associated compute facilities.

00:03:42.635 --> 00:03:48.635
falcon heavy side boosters make a clean engineering deep dive because each one is a full falcon 9 first

00:03:48.635 --> 00:03:54.195
stage flying with its own tanks and 9 merlin engines. The center core is not a twin in disguise.

00:03:54.835 --> 00:03:59.355
It holds the upper stage so the tank layout and the path that force takes through the metal are

00:03:59.355 --> 00:04:04.635
different from the side cores. Strap three of those cores together and the stack makes roughly 5

00:04:04.635 --> 00:04:09.975
million pounds of thrust at liftoff, while most of the dry hardware stays identical to the falcon 9

00:04:09.975 --> 00:04:15.735
fleet already flying. Divide that 5 million pounds across 27 Merlins and you get on the order

00:04:15.735 --> 00:04:22.835
of 185,000 pounds per engine. The same family, just more of them. In SI units, that lift-off

00:04:22.835 --> 00:04:28.495
shove is roughly 22 mega-nootons. That is the whole three-core bet. Multiply thrust without

00:04:28.495 --> 00:04:33.755
drawing a new booster from a blank sheet. Recovering the side boosters brings back most of the vehicles

00:04:33.755 --> 00:04:39.055
dry mass after every flight. And that is how kilograms to orbit get cheaper than they are on an

00:04:39.055 --> 00:04:45.895
expendable heavy. The first demonstration flight in 2018 lofted a 1,250 kilogram payload,

00:04:46.355 --> 00:04:51.895
the Tesla Roadster onto a path that went beyond Mars. Later missions showed the side boosters

00:04:51.895 --> 00:04:56.515
can return to ground pads while the center core tries for a drone ship, the autonomous

00:04:56.515 --> 00:05:02.135
barge at sea, so the recoveries are split by stage. You pay for that with extra complexity

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:06.995
at the attachment points, and you buy a fast path to heavy lift without inventing a clean

00:05:06.995 --> 00:05:12.495
sheet first stage. The same modularity now hauls national security and commercial payloads

00:05:12.495 --> 00:05:17.615
that used to need an entirely new vehicle. The magic wand number is ugly in a useful way.

00:05:18.095 --> 00:05:23.675
The raw metal, the kerosene, and the liquid oxygen in one Falcon 9 class first stage cost

00:05:23.675 --> 00:05:28.875
far less than the finished booster, which is a high idiot index, the factor by which the

00:05:28.875 --> 00:05:34.735
built part outruns its raw inputs. Reuse is the attack on that gap. Fly the side boosters

00:05:34.735 --> 00:05:39.255
home and you reclaim the tanks, the engines, and the avionics that ate most of the hardware

00:05:39.255 --> 00:05:44.435
spend. On a back-of-envelope cut, two of the three cores coming back means on the order

00:05:44.435 --> 00:05:49.615
of two-thirds of first-stage dry mass is not thrown away, even while early flights still

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:54.215
expend the center core. The finished vehicle already delivers more than twice the payload

00:05:54.215 --> 00:06:00.035
of the next competing heavy lift rocket at roughly one-third the cost per kilogram. That ratio

00:06:00.035 --> 00:06:04.355
is the argument for strapping proven cores together instead of waiting on a new stage.

00:06:04.735 --> 00:06:08.035
Attachment loads at the inner core interfaces are not a footnote.

00:06:08.495 --> 00:06:10.795
Each side booster is shoving with 9 engines,

00:06:11.235 --> 00:06:16.435
and that force has to cross into the center core through reinforced thrust structure and load sharing hardware.

00:06:16.955 --> 00:06:20.895
That hardware adds mass, which is the tax you pay for thrust multiplication,

00:06:21.575 --> 00:06:26.335
but the interfaces are built so each core can still gimbal, swivel the engines to steer,

00:06:26.855 --> 00:06:28.535
and throttle on its own during a scent.

00:06:29.135 --> 00:06:32.695
Independent throttle matters because the side boosters drop away first.

00:06:32.695 --> 00:06:37.435
The center core has to keep flying so it cannot be locked to the same thrust profile

00:06:37.435 --> 00:06:38.175
as its neighbors.

00:06:38.955 --> 00:06:44.115
Lose one merlin on a 9 engine Falcon 9 and you have dropped about 11% of first stage

00:06:44.115 --> 00:06:50.615
thrust. Lose one of 27 on heavy and the hit is on the order of 4%, which is why a clustered

00:06:50.615 --> 00:06:56.115
architecture can absorb an engine out without ending the mission. The stack can loft 64 metric

00:06:56.115 --> 00:07:02.095
tons to low earth orbit or LEO, using the same merlin family and the same kerosene and oxygen

00:07:02.095 --> 00:07:05.415
in combination already flown on hundreds of Falcon 9 missions.

00:07:05.995 --> 00:07:07.855
Heritage is the hidden, cheap ingredient.

00:07:08.375 --> 00:07:12.895
Same engines, same propellants, same ground support gear for medium lift and heavy lift,

00:07:13.335 --> 00:07:17.195
so you are not standing up a second launch enterprise to get 64 tons.

00:07:17.815 --> 00:07:23.255
Falcon 9 Block 5 upgrades can also move onto the side boosters independently, because those

00:07:23.255 --> 00:07:25.595
boosters are still Falcon 9 cores at heart.

00:07:26.175 --> 00:07:29.895
The fleet improves, and heavy inherits it without a parallel development line.

00:07:29.895 --> 00:07:35.135
Over time, the reuse logic that already applies to the side boosters is expected to reach

00:07:35.135 --> 00:07:39.895
the center core, which is how the cost floor for the heaviest payloads keeps moving down.

00:07:40.655 --> 00:07:44.295
On the public tape, shares closed higher by a little under 2%.

00:07:44.295 --> 00:07:49.735
Before we go, the thing to watch is whether Flight 15 is actually ready when its window opens.

